{
  "abstract": "We re-evaluate how gauge-profile geometry can enter gravity and cosmology. Within a declared auxiliary six-dimensional product ansatz, the dimensionless internal-volume coefficient is 20.07064 times the cube of the dimensionless circle radius. Restoring a common internal length gives the corresponding conditional Newton-scaling relation if that auxiliary manifold is adopted as the compactification. It is not the selected q79/Fu-Yau space, so the coefficient is an ansatz diagnostic rather than the current MTT internal volume. Even within the ansatz, the gauge profile does not determine Newton's constant without an absolute scale and a fundamental gravity normalization. A gauge matching point also does not select a physical coherence cutoff. The paper derives the correctly normalized conditional primordial-tensor inequality under a separately assumed cutoff and cosmological state. It supplies scaling laws and an assumption audit, not cross-sector numerical closure.",
